			<Item class="Script" referent="RBX1801">
				<Properties>
					<bool name="Disabled">false</bool>
					<Content name="LinkedSource"><null></null></Content>
					<string name="Name">READ_ME</string>
					<ProtectedString name="Source">--[[This is the Read Me
Good job on reading it.
If you&apos;re not reading it, then you&apos;re not smart enough to have to worry about editing the script.

DON&apos;T RENAME OR MOVE ANYTHING
JUST RUN THE SCRIPT AND IT&apos;LL WORK

What the script basically does is makes it so that the map appears to be &apos;dark&apos; for the players. They can only see so
far in any direction. The way this works is they are surrounded by spheres that only they can see. After that their camera
is made so that it cannot zoom out too far.

A piece of asthetic guidelines... make sure you add an ambient to make the place seem dark. ;)

All you have to do to make this script work is stick it in the workspace. Chances are, you don&apos;t even need to read this.
If you find yourself wanting to edit the &apos;darkness&apos;, just change the transparence and vertex size of the meshes of the
spheres. DO NOT RESIZE THEM.
For example, if you wanted it so that you could see farther, you&apos;d add a certain number to all three vertices of the mesh
objects.
Say that the mesh&apos;s vertices are currently 40, 40, 40. You want people to see 5 studs farther. In order to do that, you&apos;d
change the vertices to 50, 50, 50. You add TWICE the amount of distance you want people to see.
Also, if a mesh&apos;s vertices are negative, leave it as such. Only the first number has to be negative. If you make any more numbers
negative, it will just make the mesh normal again, and ruin the darkness. The sphere&apos;s are in the Lighting service.

The players camera is restricted, meaning that they can only zoom out so far. This is to prevent the player from
zooming out past the extents of the darkness. If you want to, you can remove it, but I&apos;d advise against it.
Jordanbenyon made that script, hence he is credited.
And on that note, Lance7 taught me welds, which is the basis of this script. Hence he is credited as well.

The darkness will not appear in solo. Your camera will however be restricted in solo.

If the script is &apos;broken&apos; you&apos;re doing something wrong. Just reinsert this script from your models and it oughta work fine.
Also, this script is not infected. Trust me, it was made from scratch.

And if you&apos;ve noticed the scripts make no sense... that&apos;s to stop you from stealing them. They work fine.


Don&apos;t take credit for this script.
This script was made by Samacado, with the help from Lance7 and Jordanbenyon

If you have any questions about this script, or any Samacado Studios items, feel free to
PM me or xfire me. My username on xfire is Samacado.

Thanks for using my script!
Remember, this is the original script! Anyone who claims otherwise is a liar!]]-- 
</ProtectedString>
					<bool name="archivable">true</bool>
				</Properties>
			</Item>
